    "faq_intl": {
      "type": "faq-hub",
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "International (Aramex)",
            "tags": "speed,delivery times,aramex",
            "question": "How long do international deliveries take?",
            "answer": "<p>International orders ship with Aramex and must be prepaid. <strong>GCC</strong> (Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, Bahrain, Qatar, Oman): 3–7 business days. <strong>Most other countries:</strong> 8–15 business days. <strong>Canada and North Macedonia:</strong> 7–12 business days.</p><p>Transit estimates begin after dispatch and can be affected by customs clearance, local import restrictions, public holidays or remote-area delivery.</p><p><a href=\"#track\">Track your order</a></p>",
            "sources": ""
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "International (Aramex)",
            "tags": "country estimates,gcc,rates",
            "question": "How much is international shipping?",
            "answer": "<p><strong>GCC:</strong> AED 90, free from AED 750. <strong>Most countries:</strong> AED 150, free from AED 1,200. <strong>Canada and North Macedonia:</strong> AED 260, free from AED 1,500. Rates are flat by destination. See the <a href=\"/pages/shipping-and-returns\">shipping policy</a>.</p>",
            "sources": ""
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "International (Aramex)",
            "tags": "tracking dates,reliability,eta",
            "question": "About tracking dates",
            "answer": "<p>Carrier dates are estimates and can shift with flights or customs. If your parcel goes beyond your window, contact us and we’ll assist with carrier-related delivery issues.</p>",
            "sources": ""
          }
        },
        "i4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "International (Aramex)",
            "tags": "exception,customs,hold",
            "question": "What does “Exception” mean?",
            "answer": "<p>It’s a temporary stop, often a customs check or local delivery event. Customs duties, taxes and import charges are not included unless shown at checkout. The recipient is responsible for paying applicable destination-country charges. Certain products may be restricted locally; customers confirm import eligibility.</p><p>Contact us and we’ll assist with carrier-related delivery issues. Return or redelivery costs caused by refusal, unpaid duties, an incorrect address or an unresponsive recipient may be deducted from the refund.</p>",
            "sources": ""
          }
        }
      },
